==Trivia==
*The word "Nylocas" is very similar to the Hungarian word "Nyolcas", meaning "eight", referencing the eight legs of this arachnid-like creature.
*The latter part of the name of the Nylocas Athanatos likely derives from the Greek adjective "ἀθάνατος" ("athánatos"), meaning "undying" or "immortal", referencing its background within the lore.

